			<div class="content" id="post-content-3861557">
									

<p>Funny enough, the slash fic mention was actually part of why I enjoyed this SCP. Given the circumstances, it felt like a shot at awkward humor to alleviate from the reality of her grim situation. It was also nice to see something absurd enough to relieve the story's ongoing tension, even if only for a moment in a throw-away line. It's short, notable, and characterizes the writer with a bit of personality (snarky and sarcastic, which fits the rest of her writing style) and a dash of healthy humanization. If anything, I'd question her mention of only continuing to read if we had proper clearance. It makes sense in the context of setting up the twist, but it felt out of place for her open and laid-back personality up to this point, and I wasn't sure why this would be a concern moments before her death when staff would automatically restrict her note to those with higher clearance. It was far from enough to ruin her dialogue for me, but it was notable enough to take me out of the audio to question why she was bringing it up.</p>
<p>As for containment procedures, I thought it did what it needed. No point in dragging it out, especially if containment is that simplistic. Just because it's short doesn't mean it isn't difficult, it's just that that's all you can really do to handle the entity. That's why it's Keter, after all. Overall, it was a fun read, and in my own state no less! +1</p>

							</div>

								
